# Architecture — Design Authority (Gemeente Den Haag)

Source of truth: Design Authority wiki in this repo. Prefer links over duplicating maintained content.

References: [Azure WAF](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/well-architected/) · [CAF landing zone](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/cloud-adoption-framework/ready/landing-zone/) · [MCSB](https://learn.microsoft.com/security/benchmark/azure/overview)

## Generated code readability (all languages)

- **No double dashes (`--`)** or em dashes in generated IaC/comments; use `#` or `//` comment lines.
- **Comment each module/output block** in Bicep/YAML: architectural intent (hub-spoke, PE, diagnostics), not syntax.

## Document types
| Type | When | Content |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **HLD** | Scope and directional architecture approved first | What/why, FR/NFR, logical architecture, box-level connectivity, risks, BC tiers |
| **LLTD/LLD** | After HLD (or equivalent intake) and before/during implementation | How: Azure resources, identity, network/trust boundaries, BIV, IaC/CI/CD, DR, tests, ADRs |
| **ADR** | Any architecture-impacting decision or deviation | Context, options, decision, consequences — in Architecture Decision Log |

- Every LLTD links upstream artefact in §0.1 (HLD, intake, or pattern brief). If no HLD, state replacement and approver.
- Do not duplicate HLD in LLTD; trace FR/NFR to §3–§6 and §8.
- Non-applicable LLTD sections → **Appendix 1: Not Applicable List**, then remove from body.
- Deviations from HLD, reference architecture, or landing-zone standards → ADR in §9.
- Doc changes via PR only; link work items; use relative links and [Definitions](wiki/Glossary/Definitions.md) terminology.

## LLTD workload profiles (§0)

Select **one** profile in metadata:

- **Profile A — Application workload:** app in application subscription (internal **or** citizen-facing). Subvariants: **A1** internal staff, **A2** citizen/special-category data, **A3** PaaS-only (no custom VNet).
- **Profile B — Platform automation:** pipelines, tenant-security patterns, hub/firewall/DNS. Subvariants: **B1** pattern/automation (trust-boundary + traffic summary), **B2** shared platform network (full §3.4 hub-spoke).

**Application landing zone** = application subscription (+ optional spoke VNet). Not synonymous with DigiD/Digikoppeling.

## Design Authority gates

Required: new pattern/material deviation (ADR); Profile B wiki publication; non-standard network/identity/data posture; explicit platform/Regie request.

Usually **not** required: Profile A internal app on standard ALZ baseline without ADRs; routine feature LLTD in approved boundary; Profile B deploy covered by approved pattern LLTD.

When unsure, consult Design Authority early — default is not automatic escalation.

## ADRs

- Check existing ADRs before proposing new decisions.
- Filename: `NNNN-en-short-slug.md` (sequential, language prefix).
- YAML frontmatter: Status, Date, Author, Decision makers, Consulted, Informed.
- Status: `proposed` → `accepted` | `rejected` | `deprecated` | `replaced by ADR-NNNN`.
- Minimum: context, drivers, options, outcome, consequences, confirmation criteria.

## Azure naming (CAF / GDH)

**When:** any string that becomes an **Azure resource name**, **subscription display name**, or **management group** identifier in ARM.

**Case: kebab-case** (lowercase + hyphens). Code symbols (`param`, `$var`) use **camelCase** — see `engineering.mdc`.

- American English, **lowercase**, `a-z` `0-9` hyphens only; kebab-case between segments.
- Named segments (`application`, `component`, `domain`, `environment`): **exactly 3 letters**.
- Matryoshka order: Application → Component → Environment → resource type + instance → sub-resource.
- Subscriptions add **Domain** above Application. Instance numbers zero-padded (`001`).
- Use Microsoft CAF abbreviations. Names **deterministic from parameters**. **Immutable** after create.
- Do **not** embed department, team, or region in names.
- Environments: `sbx`, `dev`, `tst`, `acc`, `prd`.

## Tagging

- Controlled vocabulary via Azure Policy; keys **Uppercase**, values **lowercase**.
- **Never** tag secrets, IPs, or PII.
- Mandatory on subscription: `Applicatienaam`, `Omgeving`, `Afdeling`, `Eigenaar`, `Kostenplaats`, `Data Classificatie`.
- `Eigenaar`: `<firstname.lastname@denhaag.nl>`.

## IaC & repositories

- IaC is the **only authoritative source** for infrastructure; manual drift must be detectable/recoverable.
- **Orchestration repo:** reusable patterns (Bicep, workflows, pipeline templates).
- **Configuration repo:** environment values, parameter files, composition pipelines (`extends` orchestration).
- Application pipelines deploy only within assigned landing-zone subscriptions.
- Document in LLTD §6.2: module layout, Key Vault refs for secrets, drift detection, policy-as-code, naming/tagging, environment parity.
- Policy changes: PR + 2 reviewers; validate in **Canary Tenant** before production.
- Baseline initiatives: **MCSB** + **NL BIO Cloud Theme V2**.

